A||N||2||johnmac||Frozen Spark Plugs Removal||||10||
Z||000000||johnmac||02-28-2000||06:53 AM||||I have 2 Frozen Spark Plugs near the firewall of my 86 GT (V6 2.8L) which cannot be removal. Feels like some nut before me rounded off the corners of the plugs.<P>Is there a special plug removal extractor available out there?<P>I have already tried rust removal, 3 & 1 oil and etc.<P>I am open to suggestions.<P>HELP<P>John MacHaffie<BR>86 GT - a few weeks to go||||reg||10
Z||000001||Tom88gt||02-28-2000||01:40 PM||||Try a 6 sided deep socket.  Many sparkplug sockets are 12 point and will slip if the plug is starting to get rounded off.  <P>If you have room, you could also try tapping an SAE socket of a slightly smaller size onto the plug.  That might compensate for the rounded corners.<P>You might also try running the engine for several minutes to heat up the heads.  The expansion of the metal may loosen the plug.  Don't know if this will work in your case but it's a good trick for many metal parts which have "frozen" together.    <P>Just be careful.  Its hard to "restore" rounded corners.  The worse the plug gets, the harder it will be to remove it.||||reg||3
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||02-28-2000||01:49 PM||||Try using a socket that grips the sides instead of the rounded off cornors on the spark plug. How do you say.....Metwrench.||||reg||1
